course: dictionary
lesson: 7964
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Recession» is one of them. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. The context is the clue.
explain: «The recession hit the shops, and many people lost their jobs.» Shops and jobs tell you this is about money and work. A recession here is a bad time for a country's businesses, when people lose jobs and spending falls.
explain: «The glacier's recession shows it is shrinking back.» Glacier and shrinking tell you this is about ice moving back, not about money. Ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check it still makes sense.
fact: Recession means a time when a country's businesses do badly.
fact: In a recession, many people lose their jobs and spending falls.
fact: «Recession» can also mean moving back or away, like a tide or a glacier going back. This meaning is formal.
fact: «A deep recession» means a very bad recession, and «the recession hit» means it started to affect people.
fact: «Soft landing» means a slowdown that avoids a full recession.
exercise: «In a recession, shops close and money is tight.» What is a recession in this sentence? | A glacier moving forward | *A time when a country's businesses do badly | A time when shops are very busy with sales | A type of tide
exercise: «The glacier's recession shows it is shrinking back.» What does recession mean here? | *Moving back or away | Making lots of money | Being very cold | Growing bigger and faster
exercise: Which phrase means a slowdown that avoids a full recession? | Deep recession | The recession hit | Economic boom | *Soft landing
test: «In a boom, jobs are easy to find, and in a recession jobs get scarcer.» In a recession, what happens to jobs? | Jobs get scarcer | Jobs are free to anyone | *Fewer jobs are available, so they are harder to find | Jobs pay more money
test: «A recession is when a country's economy shrinks for a while.» What does shrinks mean here? | *Gets smaller | Gets bigger | Turns into a boom | Stays exactly the same forever
exam: If a country's economy shrinks by 1%, what does a £100 economy become? | *£99 | £101 | £90 | £100
